  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It would be really awesome to be able to script our avatars (and worlds if udon isn't good enough) in Lua. It is almost perfect for this job. It's quite easy to use and it's very lightweight. We could add far more complex stuff to our avatars without relying on external (OSC) programs as much or destroying everyone's frame-rates with extreme amounts of animations and constraint trickery.\n\nHere are some of the extra things that could be in the API that are currently near impossible to do:\n\n-  A way to get the orientation of a grabbed PhysBone.\n\n- Texture editing.\n\n- Read certain information (like eye height and head/hand positions) about players that can be interacted with.\n\n- Set/reset avatar height.\n\n- Custom IK.",
